# Component Reuse

## Before creating a new component

1. Check whether something similar already exists under:
   - `apps/intersfrontend/src/components/`
   - the current feature folder
2. Prefer reusing or composing an existing component over copying JSX.
3. Extract a shared component only when the same UI is used in **two or more** places (or a mentor asks you to).

## Where components live

| Kind | Location |
|------|----------|
| Reusable UI (Button, Spinner, ErrorMessage) | `src/components/` |
| Feature-specific UI used once | next to the feature (e.g. under `src/` or a feature folder) |
| App shell / page | `App.jsx` or route-level files |

## Composition rules

- Keep shared components focused on one job (display a button, show an error, etc.).
- Pass data and callbacks via props; do not hardcode feature-specific API calls inside shared UI.
- Prefer composition (`<Card><UserName /></Card>`) over giant prop bags.
- Do not invent a design system library; plain React components are enough.

## Do not

- Duplicate the same button/form/status markup across files — extract instead.
- Create a new shared component for a one-off layout.
- Add UI libraries (MUI, Chakra, etc.) unless a mentor asks.
